# 1. Data Collection

This project uses the Breast Cancer Wisconsin Diagnostic dataset.
It contains measurements computed from digitized images of breast
mass samples. The objective is to compare a Decision Tree and a
Random Forest model for classifying the diagnosis as benign or malignant.

```{r packages}
packages <- c("tidyverse", "caret", "rpart", "rpart.plot",
              "randomForest", "corrplot", "pROC")

missing_packages <- packages[
  !vapply(packages, requireNamespace, logical(1), quietly=TRUE)
]

if (length(missing_packages) > 0) {
  install.packages(missing_packages, repos="https://cloud.r-project.org")
}

invisible(lapply(packages, library, character.only=TRUE))
```

```{r load-data}
raw <- read.csv("data.csv", check.names=TRUE)

cat("Dataset dimensions:", dim(raw), "\n")
head(raw)
```

# 2. Data Pre-processing and Wrangling

We remove identifier columns, check for missing values, and convert
the diagnosis into a factor for classification.

```{r preprocessing}
names(raw) <- trimws(names(raw))

if (!"diagnosis" %in% names(raw)) {
  stop("The dataset has no 'diagnosis' column. Check data.csv.")
}

df <- raw %>%
  select(-any_of(c("id", "X", "Unnamed: 32"))) %>%
  mutate(
    diagnosis = factor(
      diagnosis,
      levels=c("B", "M"),
      labels=c("Benign", "Malignant")
    )
  ) %>%
  filter(!is.na(diagnosis))

cat("Rows and columns after cleaning:", dim(df), "\n")
cat("Missing values:", sum(is.na(df)), "\n")
table(df$diagnosis)
```

```{r missing-values}
missing_summary <- colSums(is.na(df))
data.frame(
  Feature=names(missing_summary),
  MissingValues=as.integer(missing_summary)
)
```

# 3. Exploratory and Inferential Analysis

